# 0007. Per-project env via direnv `layout project`, secrets in sops-encrypted .env

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

## Context
Projects need their own variables and Python virtualenvs, and some variables are secrets that
should still be shareable through git.

## Decision
`direnv/direnvrc` defines `layout project`: loads `.env` (git-ignored everywhere), `.env.sops`
(decrypted in memory with sops + age), and activates `.venv`/`venv`. A project's `.envrc` is that
one line (`envinit` writes it).

## Alternatives
- Per-project `.envrc` logic: copied and drifting between projects.
- Plain `.env` only: secrets can't be committed or shared.

## Consequences
- Same setup in every project; encrypted secrets can live in git.
- Needs an age key per person (`make age-key`), backed up: without it `.env.sops` can't be read.

## References
`direnv/direnvrc`, `Makefile` (`age-key`).
